tests/ui/types/err_attribute_on_value.sky:4:9: error: a vector has no attribute `mean`
  |
4 | print(x.mean())
  |         ^^^^ no such attribute
  = help: Sky has no methods, and no `mean` function yet; a sum over the entries can be written as a loop over `range(len(x))`

tests/ui/types/err_attribute_on_value.sky:5:9: error: a matrix has no attribute `T`
  |
5 | print(A.T)
  |         ^ no such attribute
  = help: write `Aᵀ` for the transpose

tests/ui/types/err_attribute_on_value.sky:6:9: error: a vector has no attribute `T`
  |
6 | print(x.T)
  |         ^ no such attribute
  = help: a vector has no row or column orientation, so there is nothing to transpose: `u @ v` is already the dot product

tests/ui/types/err_attribute_on_value.sky:7:9: error: a vector has no attribute `shape`
  |
7 | print(x.shape)
  |         ^^^^^ no such attribute
  = help: write `len(x)` for its length

tests/ui/types/err_attribute_on_value.sky:8:9: error: a matrix has no attribute `foo`
  |
8 | print(A.foo)
  |         ^^^ no such attribute
  = help: Sky values have no attributes or methods: functions are called as `f(x)`
